@startuml ETLAgentLifecycleSequence
title ETL-Agent Generation and Governed Execution
autonumber

actor Maker
actor Checker1
actor Checker2
actor Operator
participant API as "FastAPI Control Plane"
participant Graph as "LangGraph Workflow"
participant LLM as "Bailian LLM Provider"
database DB as "PostgreSQL"
participant PDP as "Policy Decision Point"
participant Broker as "Tool Broker"
queue Outbox
participant Worker as "Celery Worker"
participant Engine as "SeaTunnel Zeta"
participant Target as "Target Database"

Maker -> API: POST generation(request)
API -> Graph: start AgentRun
Graph -> DB: load Profile + checkpoint
Graph -> LLM: structured generation(redacted profile)
LLM --> Graph: EtlPlan/HOCON candidate
Graph -> Graph: schema + deterministic gate
alt missing parameter or invalid candidate
  Graph --> API: interrupt(question/errors)
  API --> Maker: clarification request
  Maker -> API: POST answer
  API -> Graph: resume checkpoint
else gate passed
  Graph -> DB: freeze PipelineVersion + SHA-256
  Graph --> API: candidate ready
end

Maker -> API: POST prepare(version)
API -> PDP: decide(ToolIntent, scope, classification)
PDP --> API: risk + required role slots
API -> DB: freeze Preparation
API --> Maker: Preparation

Checker1 -> API: approve(data dimension)
API -> DB: ApprovalRequest decision
Checker2 -> API: approve(security dimension)
API -> DB: ApprovalRequest decision

Operator -> API: POST commit(preparation)
API -> DB: verify fingerprint + approvals
API -> Broker: issue single-use Capability
Broker -> DB: transaction(ExecutionRun + Outbox)
Broker --> API: execution_run_id
Outbox -> Worker: deliver authorized command
Worker -> Broker: verify Capability + replay guard
Worker -> Engine: submit bounded job
Engine -> Target: shadow write + error routing
Engine --> Worker: metrics/status
Worker -> DB: snapshots + audit events

alt quality passed
  Worker -> Engine: atomic swap
else budget exceeded or failure
  Worker -> Engine: cancel / cleanup / rollback
end
Worker --> API: final status + quality report
API --> Operator: execution result
@enduml
